iption":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-05-19T17:29:43Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T10:25:58Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducable in all major Godot 4.0 Versions.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev4 - Linux Mint 22.1 (Xia) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti (nvidia; 570.133.07) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using a SeparationRayShape2D for collision, it will report collisions with one way objects, even though the report shouldnt allow for it, when the angles are opposing.\n\nthis means that if a characters collision is made of seperation rays, it means that one way collision, simply does not work.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nattach a characterbody2d with a sepearation ray shape with a direction opposite of a one way collisions, angle.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[SeparationRayBug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20301534/SeparationRayBug.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106603/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106603/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}